          explanation: 'The Sundara Kanda — the "beautiful" chapter — is the heart of the Ramayana because it is about the triumph of devotion and focused purpose. Hanuman alone undertakes the impossible journey across the ocean. He succeeds because he has one clear intention and complete surrender to a higher cause.',
          science: 'Research on intrinsic motivation and goal-pursuit (Self-Determination Theory): when a person acts from a deep sense of purpose and genuine devotion (as opposed to fear or external pressure), their cognitive resources integrate, obstacles reduce anxiety, and performance reaches its peak. Hanuman\'s journey is a narrative model of purpose-driven peak performance.',
